From 8a8716d016c60d6a2640108ba686b5752466f3c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:05:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ui): machined mesh paints deviation classes and lights
 the hovered facet

The extracted machined mesh (M13.1) now carries the Deviate legend:
each facet is judged once per mesh by the GPU eye's own law - the
model's DistanceLattice read at the facet centroid, gated by
gate_tol(DEV_TOL, cell) - into clean / rest / gouge / unjudged
(app::machined_classes, cached in MeshCache::classify next to the mesh,
primed with the extraction). The scene expands the classes to the stock
part's per-vertex buffer, so the mesh paints the same colours as the
sheet and the traced eye.

A stock hover answered by the mesh keeps the triangle it hit
(State::hover_mesh, view state, never a command); the shell draws it as
a hover-yellow veil and outline projected through the camera each frame.

Decision: docs/decisions/25-mesh-hover-deviation.md

Fixes #25

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
